# The desktop OPTIONS screen — the D9 flat row list.
#
# Attract -> main menu -> down onto OPTIONS -> open. The single `key down`
# assumes the NETLESS build the shots README tells you to make
# (`make NETPLAY=0`), whose menu is NEW GAME / OPTIONS: a netplay build
# inserts ONLINE between them (menu.cpp draw order) and this scene would
# render the online chooser instead, so add a second `key down` there. A
# save file adds CONTINUE on top and shifts it again.
#
# Netless also means 8 option rows, not 9 — `net_board_available()`
# drops LEADERBOARD UPLOAD. For the 9-row list force that predicate true
# in a local build; the ONLINE row stays hidden either way, since it keys
# on net_available() instead. The 16-row worst case the D9/O5 row budget
# was judged on no longer lives here: the zoom work moved the per-player
# camera rows one level down, and camera.shot renders that sub-screen.
seed 3
menu
sim 1800
key enter 200
key down 700
key enter 1200
